{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a local caching DNS resolver on node1 and configure system applications to use it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unbound was active, enabled, and listening only on IPv4/IPv6 loopback port 53. NetworkManager generated resolv.conf with 127.0.0.1 and ::1; default dig used 127.0.0.1, and controlled queries directly demonstrated a cache miss followed by a cache hit and 0 ms response. The service, settings, listeners, and caching behavior recovered after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-48fcaf0244284f23","cmd-7f2975ea235b4934","cmd-1bf97e2402834628","cmd-ab0a21b5315e4e13","cmd-8a858e7f819d43ea"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve normal external name resolution for applications on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"External resolution worked before the change, then both dig and the application-facing getent path resolved external names through the local resolver. Equivalent resolution succeeded again after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-56034748197544ff","cmd-1bf97e2402834628","cmd-227a6d1b36b64773","cmd-ab0a21b5315e4e13"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so none remained or required reversion. Installation, resolver and NetworkManager configuration, activation, and reboot were directly task-related. The first bounded service restart exposed an approximately 35-second startup-anchor delay; the subsequent adjustment and restart validated recovery, while a standalone anchor update confirmed that maintenance path still worked. Cache flushes and queries were bounded evidence actions. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, only intended loopback DNS listeners, and no executor residue beyond normal boot-specific temporary directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d9742c19f1dc4ed8","cmd-0d0807945e7b4a4e","cmd-e04fd174f2be4391","cmd-3739e517e05b4236","cmd-816e0502a7374cf7","cmd-ace8adf7f6aa4ed9","cmd-13b2e2f036fe4f0f","cmd-f3eac40534124591","cmd-7d2fedaeddde4fb9","cmd-aceb337dcf444f92","cmd-ce90446abfda46c3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both public task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory restart protocol is also complete for the sole managed node: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the reboot was acknowledged and observed taking down the command stream, a different boot identity followed, and service, configuration, external resolution, and caching all recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
